SEC. 51P-832.116. SIDEWALKS.

(a) Except as provided in this section, sidewalks must be provided as required by the Dallas Development Code. Sidewalks must be compliant with the Americans With Disabilities Act.

(1) For Tract 1, sidewalks and unobstructed sidewalk widths must be provided as shown on the Tract 1 development plan/Tract 2 conceptual plan.

(2) The following are not considered obstructions for calculating minimum unobstructed sidewalk width:

(A) public and private utility improvements including fire hydrants, power poles, and street lights;

(B) street curbs;

(C) tree grates;

(D) signalization;

(E) regulatory signs;

(F) building entrances;

(G) car overhangs;

(H) necessary appurtenances such as site steps and railings due to grading requirements; and

(I) planters.

(3) The unobstructed sidewalk may traverse through an area or under a covered arcade or architectural element provided a minimum ten feet of unobstructed vertical clearance is provided.

(b) No waivers or variances may be granted to the sidewalk requirements of this section. (Ord. 28032)
